1
00:00:00,079 --> 00:00:01,779
Welcome to Rez grid Academy.

2
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:06,469
In this lesson, we will understand
ai availability and human review.

3
00:00:07,079 --> 00:00:11,310
AI product descriptions and code can
move ahead of deployment availability,

4
00:00:11,590 --> 00:00:15,159
so training must distinguish
released tools from planned ones.

5
00:00:15,630 --> 00:00:18,569
We will explain the features,
the setup decisions, and a

6
00:00:18,569 --> 00:00:20,520
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:20,679 --> 00:00:24,730
An administrator asks Admin Assist
why a member was not paged and

8
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:26,299
reviews the evidence it links to.

9
00:00:26,929 --> 00:00:30,360
Get explanations and drafts
for people to review, alongside

10
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:31,999
the tools you already use.

11
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:35,879
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:35,879 --> 00:00:38,090
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:38,319 --> 00:00:39,470
Enhanced AI.

14
00:00:39,999 --> 00:00:43,270
AI assistance beyond the
free Admin Assist allowance.

15
00:00:43,649 --> 00:00:47,399
Nothing to set up yet; your free Admin
Assist allowance works without it.

16
00:00:47,849 --> 00:00:50,590
This feature is marked
planned in the source catalog.

17
00:00:51,040 --> 00:00:54,979
Verify release availability before
recording a configuration walkthrough.

18
00:00:55,259 --> 00:00:58,779
The checkout contains gated AI
dispatch settings for enrichment

19
00:00:58,779 --> 00:01:03,140
fields, confidence, sender scope,
token limits, and activity.

20
00:01:03,599 --> 00:01:07,729
Confirm host enablement and department
rollout before reviewing the settings.

21
00:01:08,099 --> 00:01:10,889
Saving settings alone
does not start enrichment.

22
00:01:11,240 --> 00:01:14,450
Check the Running state,
activity outcomes, and usage.

23
00:01:14,839 --> 00:01:18,349
This source-present feature is
unverified on the target deployment.

24
00:01:18,730 --> 00:01:21,480
Confirm availability in
the demo department before

25
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:22,900
recording the live workflow.

26
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:25,939
For the training scenario,
work in this order.

27
00:01:26,409 --> 00:01:26,979
Step 1.

28
00:01:27,549 --> 00:01:32,059
Use deterministic Setup Wizard and
Setup Report for configuration guidance.

29
00:01:32,489 --> 00:01:33,170
Step 2.

30
00:01:33,710 --> 00:01:37,069
Check whether Admin AI is enabled
for the target department.

31
00:01:37,540 --> 00:01:38,290
Step 3.

32
00:01:38,769 --> 00:01:43,249
Check release and rollout before
teaching Enhanced AI summaries or drafts.

33
00:01:43,410 --> 00:01:44,899
Now verify the result.

34
00:01:45,289 --> 00:01:49,180
Record the target deployment version
and observed feature availability.

35
00:01:49,610 --> 00:01:54,210
Human reviewers remain responsible for
any generated explanation or draft.

36
00:01:54,649 --> 00:01:58,219
A common problem to watch for:
The catalog in this checkout

37
00:01:58,219 --> 00:02:00,259
marks Enhanced AI as planned.

38
00:02:00,650 --> 00:02:05,450
This lesson explains its scope; it does
not demonstrate a released configuration.

39
00:02:05,659 --> 00:02:07,220
Your practice task is simple.

40
00:02:07,699 --> 00:02:11,330
Ask a configuration question
through an available tool, inspect

41
00:02:11,330 --> 00:02:15,339
its evidence, and identify any
unknowns before making a change.

42
00:02:15,749 --> 00:02:19,690
Record the result, who owns the
follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

43
00:02:20,089 --> 00:02:23,489
Use the linked feature scripts for
the detailed screen recording plan.
